        "title": "Block IP addresses by Username - ForcepointNGFW",
        "description": "This is forcepoint FUID playbook for blocking IP addresses by username ForcepointNGFW.",
        "mainSteps": [ "1. Fetches a list of potentially suspicious User Accounts that are part of Azure Active Directory (AAD) through Azure Sentinel.", "2. If the IP address is not present in the security policy rule then adds to the security policy and closes the incident." ],
        "prerequisites": [
            "1. Forcepoint SMC Custom Connector needs to be deployed prior to the deployment of this playbook under the same resource group.",
            "2. Forcepoint SMC API Key should be known.[Refer here](http://www.websense.com/content/support/library/ngfw/v610/rfrnce/ngfw_6100_ug_smc-api_a_en-us.pdf )",
            "3. Forcepoint SMC Version number should be known. [Refer here](https://help.stonesoft.com/onlinehelp/StoneGate/SMC/)",
            "4. Forcepoint FUID service endpoint should be known. (e.g.  https://forcepointdomain:PortNumber/})",
            "5. IP address list name for blocking IP address present in SMC should be known."
        ],
